message: "If you use this code or the archived results, please cite it as below."
title: "toyworld: testbed and pre-registered comparison of a harm-coupled alert and a prediction-error CUSUM"
type: software
version: "1.0-paper"
date-released: 2026-11-24
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/29wtd2xs8g-cmd/World1-"
authors:
  - family-names: "Jouan"
    given-names: "Alphonse"
    affiliation: "MSc in Cognitive Science (Cog-SUP), Sorbonne Université and Université Paris-Cité, Paris, France"
abstract: >-
  A toy navigation world with hidden drift and irreversible damage, the code of two
  revision triggers (a harm-coupled alert and a CUSUM on prediction error), the frozen
  pre-registration protocol and ledgers, and the raw results of the final study on the test
  seeds. Companion of the paper "When Should a Continual World Model Revise Itself?
  Margin-Coupled Nociceptive Alerts vs. Prediction Error".
keywords:
  - continual world models
  - change detection
  - CUSUM
  - safe reinforcement learning
  - nociception
  - pre-registration
  - negative result
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24502320
